LICENSE next to this file.

What changed from upstream:

- Vendored subset: only the skills, prompts and scripts this flow uses are
  copied (brainstorming, writing-plans, subagent-driven-development,
  using-git-worktrees, requesting-code-review, finishing-a-development-branch,
  systematic-debugging, test-driven-development,
  verification-before-completion, receiving-code-review,
  dispatching-parallel-agents, using-superpowers). The visual companion,
  executing-plans, writing-skills, the per-task reviewer, creation logs and
  pressure tests, the manifests of other harnesses and run-hook.cmd are not
  copied.
- Adaptations: brainstorming writes plan.md with a scope ladder and stops at
  one gate; writing-plans writes implementation-plan.md for the agreed rung
  only; subagent-driven-development runs one implementer per chunk and one
  whole-diff reviewer with at most two fix rounds; finishing-a-development-branch
  lands without a menu; plans live under docs/plans; the plan lifecycle script
  ticket.py and its templates come from the workbench plugin. UPSTREAM.md lists
  the adaptations per skill.
- Em dashes (U+2014) in vendored text are replaced by " - "; LICENSE is the
  one file kept byte for byte.
